{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374985-interesting-custom-conditions-in-your-mage-games","id":1374985,"title":"Interesting Custom Conditions In Your Mage Games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-15T15:45:00-07:00","id":1374985,"title":"Interesting Custom Conditions In Your Mage Games","content":"Here are some I made.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dance Of The Spheres (Persistent, Arcane)</b></u><br /> <i>Your mystical stargazing has revealed profound secrets about the angles and curvature of the celestial firmament, giving you a greater spatial awareness and coordination for mundane and arcane purposes. You gain a +2 on all rolls involving the Space Arcanum and Wits. However, your fixation on the heavens has left you overly reliant on their guidance for orienting yourself. If you do not spend at least 1 uninterrupted hour each day stargazing, your Perception rolls are reduced to a fixed chance die until you next stargaze.<br /> Beat: Ignore, abandon or otherwise compromise your obligations and responsibilities so you can stargaze.<br /> Resolution: Summon an Imp (i.e. Supernal Demon of Space) with a Rank equal to your Space Arcanum and complete its Trial.</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Reptilian Regeneration (Persistent, Arcane)</b></u><br /> <i>Your genetic experiments have left a mark on your own DNA, allowing you to heal at amazing speeds. You heal 1 bashing each turn, 1 lethal each hour and 1 aggravated each day. However, your reptilian brain is kicked into overdrive, which makes you think of all social interactions in terms of predator/prey dynamics. Whenever you attempt to engage with others on equal terms, your Impression Level for Social Maneuvering is Hostile unless you succeed on a roll of Resolve + Composure - Life, which suppresses your bestial instincts for the scene.<br /> Beat: Resort to Hard Leverage in a highly inadvisable situation in order to get what you want.<br /> Resolution: Subject yourself to a Life Ruling spell which prevents you from taking any aggressive actions for (10 - Wisdom) days.</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Gnarled Roots Of Friendship (Persistent, Arcane)</b></u><br /> <i>Your deep glimpse into the hearts and minds of those you hold dear has given you a superlative understanding of how their psyches work. Receive Rote Quality on all Empathy rolls involving your Cabalmates. However, such a profound connection has left you overly passionate about protecting them. Gain an additional Vice of Protective, and in any scene you regain Willpower from it, add your Empathy rating to all Paradox.<br /> Beat: Resort to overly forceful or reckless methods of protecting your Cabal.<br /> Resolution: Willingly stand aside to let a Cabalmate solve a dangerous situation on their own merits.</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Isolating Insight (Persistent, Arcane)</b></u><br /> <i>Your Mage is incredibly talented at solving Mysteries. All rolls for Scrutiny and Revelation receive 8 Again. However, he is also intensely detached from the non-Awakened mindset. When rolling for Social Maneuvering against the non-Awakened, his dice pool has a hard limit of [Wisdom] after factoring bonuses and penalties, his Impression Level is one lower and he must open additional Doors equal to his Gnosis.<br /> Beat: You suffer significant setbacks when trying to deal with non-Awakened society.<br /> Resolution: Complete a Long Term Aspiration to meaningfully bond with a Sleeper.</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Fey Charm (Persistent, Arcane)</b></u><br /> <i>Your bargains with Changelings have given you insight into their illusions, but have marked you with a certain trickster-dharma yourself. Gain a +2 to all Mind and Manipulation rolls. However, you suffer 1 Resistant Lethal every time you tell an outright lie rather than twisting words.<br /> Beat: Be deceitful and underhanded in order to avoid taking damage as described above.<br /> Resolution: Subject yourself to a Mind Ruling spell which forces you to only tell the truth for (10 - Wisdom) days.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T06:08:06-07:00","id":1375074,"title":"","content":"These are very interesting. I could see some possible balance issues, but honestly those are mostly minor and can be ignored. I think the biggest question on my mind about these is how do you acquire them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T09:21:43-07:00","id":1375098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374985-interesting-custom-conditions-in-your-mage-games?p=1375074#post1375074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are very interesting. I could see some possible balance issues, but honestly those are mostly minor and can be ignored. I think the biggest question on my mind about these is how do you acquire them?</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on context. It is usually the result of an Exceptional Success on a thematically-linked spellcasting, or prolonged/intense exposure to a specific type of Mystery. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T09:51:57-07:00","id":1375106,"title":"","content":"Never had any that fun, did have a custom one come up in a mage campaign but isn't per say specific to &quot;mage&quot; per say.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dominant Eye Destroyed (Persistent)</b></u><br /> <i>Your missing your dominant eye, Limiting your vision and depth perception, While you can still see for most mundane purposes taxing actions involving sight and movement become more difficult.<br /> Checks involving sight your rolls loose the 10again quality and 1's subtract from successes.<br /> Beat: You suffer a setback or are otherwise impaired due to your loss of vision.<br /> Resolution: Characters sight is restored.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:45:54-07:00","id":1380757,"title":"","content":"More instances from my Chronicle. You could most likely make a generic template for Arcane Conditions following these examples.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Exquisite Fleshcrafting</b></i></u><br /> <i>Resolve this Condition to receive 8 Again on any Life spell that is specifically meant for genetic modification. Alternatively, increase the Primary Factor of said spell by one step automatically. If you spend a Reach to change Primary Factor from Potency into Duration or vice-versa, you apply the Condition to the new Primary Factor.</i><br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Blazing Heart</b></i></u><br /> <i>Resolve this Condition to receive 8 Again on any Mind spell that is specifically meant for inspiring decisive action. Alternatively, increase the Primary Factor of said spell by one step automatically. If you spend a Reach to change Primary Factor from Potency into Duration or vice-versa, you apply the Condition to the new Primary Factor.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-12-2020, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:10:02-07:00","id":1405923,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Psycho-Spiritual Overflow (Persistent, Arcane)</b></i></u><br /> <i>Your Mage has a loose control over his emotions, which represents an ever-present risk for his Wisdom. Whenever your Mage regains Willpower from his Vice, is prevented from fulfilling an Aspiration/Obsession, or uses Pattern Scouring to remove an emotion-based Condition, the ST places a token on his character sheet. Once per Chapter, if the ST has accumulated tokens equal to the Mage's Wisdom, he can apply the Rampant Condition to him for the rest of the scene. This resets the number of tokens to zero. <br /> <br /> Your Mage is overwhelmed by his current emotional state, which shapes his every Imago and removes his any of his usual inhibitions regarding the harmful and destructive use of magic. He retains enough awareness to distinguish friend from foe and can Contain Paradox, but otherwise acts in accordance with what whatever emotion is taking control of him. Any rolls for Wisdom Degeneration are postponed to the end of the scene. <br /> <br /> Beat: The player requests the Rampant Condition during a dramatic moment. The player can accept the Fugue Condition as well, effectively allowing his Mage to suffer a trance-like state of superlative emotion. This is analogous to downgrading a Failure into a Dramatic Failure, and therefore grants an additional Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> Resolution: Gain an Exceptional Success on a roll for Wisdom Degeneration while under the effects of this Condition. Alternatively, change one of your Obsessions into &quot;Use Magic In A Disciplined And Methodical Way&quot; or equivalent. You Resolve this Condition upon acquiring Arcane Beats from said Obsession equal to [11 - Wisdom].</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}